  "stem": "A print shop's daily profit, in dollars, from printing \\(x\\) hundred flyers is modeled by \\(P(x) = -x^{2} + 16x - 39\\). The shop breaks even, with a daily profit of 0 dollars, for two values of \\(x\\). What is the greater of these two values?",
  "figure": null,
  "answer_type": "spr",
  "choices": null,
  "answer": null,
  "spr_answers": [
    "13"
  ],
  "solution": [
    "Set \\(P(x) = 0\\): \\(-x^{2} + 16x - 39 = 0\\), so \\(x^{2} - 16x + 39 = 0\\).",
    "Factor: \\((x - 3)(x - 13) = 0\\), so \\(x = 3\\) or \\(x = 13\\).",
    "The greater value is 13."
  ],
  "explanation": null,
  "traps": null,
  "verify": "x = symbols('x')\ns = sorted(solve(Eq(-x**2 + 16*x - 39, 0), x))\nassert s == [3, 13]\nassert Rational(spr_answers[0]) == s[-1]",
